Widen DrakeParseTest's mods scope to the whole mods tree

Dev accepted, in these words: "Accepted, build it" — the recommendation being to widen DrakeParseTest's mods walk
from the example directory to the whole of `src/mods/resources`, the move DrakeGenTest took in 8746ecd, keeping its
two filters (an authored `.drake`, no unsupported codec clause) and its two gates unchanged, rewording its comments
from "the mods actors" to the mods definitions, and moving the two §1 table rows in the same commit: parse scope
110 draco + 73 mods, surface losses 0 across 183 types. No engine, definition or Scala change; no new suite.

Why. After 8746ecd the EMIT direction of every mods surface is a gate, but the parser's two round-trip gates —
`emit(parse(source))` reproduces the surface, `parse(emit(td))` reproduces the definition — and the surface-loss
measurement still walked `domains` alone, as they had since the actor-emission increment of 2026-09-10. The 25
staged definitions under `src/mods/resources/draco` (the dreams Editor, Initialization, the User requests, the
service types, Yaml) sat outside all three. The dreams and service suites pin 24 of the 25 by hand-listed name,
and in one direction only: `Drake.emit(definition) == source` and `Drake.emit(Drake.parse(source)) == source`;
only two Service members have the parsed JSON compared with the committed JSON (ServiceTest), and Yaml, whose
surface is a day old, is pinned by nothing in the parse direction. A hand list also admits a staged definition
silently, as it admitted Yaml for the whole of its life; a walk does not.

